{"content": "First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1 is the 5th episode of the 1st season and the  5th episode overall of the Attack on Titan anime, produced by Wit Studio and Production I.G.\n\nEren's fight with the Colossal Titan comes to an abrupt halt when the creature vanishes without a trace. The cadets are entrusted with the defense of the city, causing many to panic or lose hope, and Mikasa worries for Eren's life. When the battle begins, Eren's squad is quickly decimated by the invading Titans. Armin is saved from the brink of death by Eren, but Eren is eaten in his place.\n\nWhile Eren is running on top of the Wall, the Colossal Titan charges at him, destroying the upper portion of it. Eren sees that the Titan aimed for the cannons, realizing that the gate being destroyed is not a coincidence either - the Colossal Titan is intelligent. With his omni-directional mobility gear, Eren rushes towards his opponent, while dodging the Titan's slow attack. However, just as Eren is about to strike a fatal blow, the Colossal Titan releases a huge amount of hot steam, slowing Eren down. Eren attempts to approach his target one more time, but as he tries to slash with his blades, he realizes there is no contact - the Colossal Titan has disappeared.", "chunk_index": 0, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/First_Battle:_The_Struggle_for_Trost,_Part_1", "source_title": "First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 5, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 5, "embedding": [-0.08736776560544968, 0.026197057217359543, 0.05364777892827988, 0.032936546951532364, 0.07721290737390518, -0.0017531608464196324, 0.0616195984184742, 0.037231314927339554, -0.010839259251952171, 0.028675800189375877, -0.008471528068184853, -0.02546699158847332, -0.007527106441557407, 0.0058748056180775166, -0.08554121106863022, -0.05002704635262489, 0.014420985244214535, -0.03983413055539131, 0.04973580315709114, -0.008030512370169163, 0.008