{"content": "The soldiers quickly begin their attempts at dealing with the Titans, not wanting to repeat the hell from five years ago. While the civilians continue their evacuation, the new recruits are preparing to head into action. Armin panics, claiming that the Titans can annihilate them at any time. Elsewhere, Dot Pyxis plays chess with Lord Wald at his residence. Wald complains that in spite of playing him every month, Pyxis still fails to improve. At that moment, a soldier barges into the room, announcing that the Colossal Titan destroyed the gate at Trost District. Pyxis stands up, taking Wald's bottle of booze. Revealing that he intends to go to Trost, Wald tries to stop him, claiming that his duty is to protect him and his property. However, that has no effect as Pyxis immediately leaves.\n\nAt Trost, Woermann gives orders to the cadets, dividing them into individual groups. After telling them the objective - to protect the evacuating civilians - he dismisses them. Most of the soldiers are in a state of panic or despair just as Jean walks through the area, annoyed, knowing that he was supposed to go to the interior next day. He bumps into Eren, which enrages him even more. However, Eren makes him remember how they survived their training, claiming that they will come out of this alive as well. As Jean leaves, Eren is approached by Mikasa who tells him to look for her in case of trouble. However, they are interrupted by Ian Dietrich who tells Mikasa that she has been specially assigned to the rear squad. Mikasa tries to argue, however, Eren snaps at her, saying that nobody cares about what she wants as it is mankind that is in danger right now. As they are about to part, Mikasa asks Eren not to die.", "chunk_index": 1, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/First_Battle:_The_Struggle_for_Trost,_Part_1", "source_title": "First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 5, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 5, "embedding": [-0.03692073002457619, 0.06130995601415634, -0.012803115881979465, -0.0705144926905632, 0.11212576925754547, -0.027903495356440544, 0.10747546702623367, 0.017025474458932877, 0.03165656328201294, 0.02170439250767231, -0.055976737290620804, 0.0930427834391594, 0.03320248797535896, -0.011246840469539165, 0.023736119270324707, -0.048586856573820114, -0.013187812641263008, -0.026417406275868416, 0.032781362533569336, -0.014562766999006271, 0.01820608228445053, -0.02266441471874714, 0.09187450259923935, 0.04339015856385231, -0.08548477292060852, -0.04079577326774597, 0.03977077081799507, -0.01038630586117506, -0.01976441591978073, -0.011349083855748177, -0.004655676428228617, -0.01915949210524559, -0.03870584815740585, -0.04853324592113495, -0.06366269290447235, 0.20167852938175201, 0.07160010933876038, -0.007616404443979263, -0.0588332936167717, 0.0034817708656191826, 0.0700007975101471, -0.022468937560915947, -0.029853010550141335, -0.04274895042181015, -0.01296109240502119, 0.014598796144127846, -0.043037738651037216, -0.022556517273187637, 0.050810255110263824, 0.010071178898215294, -0.010961188934743404, -0.012293044477701187, 0.0715131163597107, -0.04902197793126106, -0.029612448066473007, 0.07049281895160675, 0.030124938115477562, -0.06342914700508118, 0.06400438398122787, -0.05970233678817749, -0.05252193659543991, 0.05342577025294304, 0.04089666157960892, 0.04642331227660179, 0.00368310883641243, -0.033826425671577454, -0.016111062839627266, -0.026152288541197777, -0.02210899256169796, 0.07843741774559021, 0.08676541596651077, 0.03845326974987984, -0.02745797485113144, -0.09076915681362152, -0.08134829998016357, 0.05502966418862343, 0.02453193999826908, -0.07477308064699173, -0.016089772805571556, -0.008184758946299553, -0.003859467338770628, -0.03916573524475098, 0.0285131074488163, 0.007654496934264898, -0.00906331930309534, 0.017501913011074066, 0.030030585825443268, -0.07373374700546265, 0.06208415329456329, -0.0017653239192441106, 0.04409