{"content": "Some time later, Eren recalls his time as a member of the 104th Cadet Corps. In a class, a lecture commandant is reading a book about Titans, revealing information about them. Eren is seen shocked to hear about their regeneration, them not needing to eat or their unknown means of reproduction. When the commandant is questioned whether the Titans are invulnerable, he reveals their weak spot - the nape of their neck and the two blades used to slice through it. Back in the present, Eren and Armin are standing by, waiting for orders.\n\nEren claims that this is their chance as doing well in the operation before even joining the Scout Regiment will surely lead into their promotion. The rest of his squad is also eager to prove themselves. At that moment, they are ordered to assist the front guards. Running through the city, they find out that the Titans are already inside. Suddenly, they are targeted by an Abnormal Titan that jumps at them. Thinking they have evaded it, the group realizes that it is Thomas being held in the Titan's mouth. Before he can react, the Titan devours him, much to the horror of his teammates.", "chunk_index": 2, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/First_Battle:_The_Struggle_for_Trost,_Part_1", "source_title": "First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 5, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 5, "embedding": [-0.12072616815567017, 0.04852791130542755, 0.0402725413441658, 0.015017270110547543, 0.10335853695869446, -0.029184691607952118, 0.10022766143083572, 0.014572924003005028, -0.034391023218631744, 0.03905243054032326, 0.04044211283326149, 0.033298321068286896, 0.03245589882135391, 0.01424373034387827, -0.026846207678318024, -0.036295000463724136, -0.026133766397833824, -0.008312065154314041, -0.059292301535606384, 0.03808987885713577, -0.02613753452897072, 0.03313540667295456, 0.04642287269234657, 0.05597369372844696, -0.041724804788827896, -0.06963470578193665, -0.02826